{"seq":3,"slug":"writing-docs-for-both","title":"Writing Docs For Both","docCount":3,"url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/writing-docs-for-both","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"clear-structured-discoverable","title":"清晰、有结构、可发现","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/writing-docs-for-both/clear-structured-discoverable","wordCount":1952,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"keeping-docs-close-to-code","title":"让文档贴近代码","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/writing-docs-for-both/keeping-docs-close-to-code","wordCount":1949,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"examples-and-runnable-docs","title":"例子与可运行的文档","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/writing-docs-for-both/examples-and-runnable-docs","wordCount":1867,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章讲怎么把文档写得既帮人也帮 agent——好消息是,对两者好的写法基本一致。清晰、有结构、可发现:用清晰的标题分节、明确的层次,让人能扫读、agent 能定位,放在标准位置、被索引,确保找得到。贴近代码:让文档离它描述的代码近(同一仓库、就近目录、随代码一起改),近,既好发现也好保持同步——离得越远越容易过期。例子与可运行的文档:具体的例子比抽象描述好懂得多,agent 能直接照着用;能跑、能被验证的文档(可执行的例子、文档化的命令)还能不静默过期——跑不通就暴露,胜过一段没人知道已经错了的描述。\n"}